WEBVTT

00:03:29.329 --> 00:03:34.288
posed a new risk called 
“the superparamagnetic effect”.

00:03:35.288 --> 00:03:37.579
When a magnetic grain volume is too small,

00:03:37.621 --> 00:03:41.121
its magnetization is easily
disturbed by heat energy

00:03:41.163 --> 00:03:43.663
and can cause bits
to switch unintentionally,

00:03:43.704 --> 00:03:46.704
leading to data loss.

00:03:46.746 --> 00:03:50.288
Scientists resolved this limitation
in a remarkably simple way:

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:55.954
by changing the direction of recording
from longitudinal to perpendicular,

00:03:55.996 --> 00:04:00.996
allowing areal density to approach
one terabit per square inch.